---
source: crates/pogo-cli/tests/cli.rs
expression: help
---
List connected serial devices and classify them

Usage: pogo devices [OPTIONS]

Options:
      --all
          Also show unrecognized serial devices

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

  -V, --version
          Print version

Global options:
  -d, --device <SELECTOR>
          Target device: alias, USB serial, port, or "auto"

      --probe <SELECTOR>
          Probe device [default: "probe" alias, else auto]

  -f, --format <FORMAT>
          Output format [default: human]
          
          [env: POGO_FORMAT=]
          [possible values: human, json, jsonl]

      --config <PATH>
          Config file
          
          [env: POGO_CONFIG=]

      --timeout <DURATION>
          Overall deadline for this command, e.g. 500ms, 10s, 2m

      --wait-lock <DURATION>
          Wait for a busy device instead of failing

      --dry-run
          Describe what a mutating command would do; change nothing

  -v, --verbose...
          More logs on stderr (repeatable)

  -q, --quiet
          Errors only on stderr

      --no-color
          Disable colors

Never opens ports, so it is fast and always safe.

Examples:
  pogo devices
  pogo devices --all -f json

Exit codes: 0 ok, 10 config invalid

JSON data: { devices: [ { alias, kind, port, usb: { vid, pid, serial_number, manufacturer,
product }, chip_hint, locked_by } ] }. kind is esp32_target, pogo_probe, or unknown_serial
(the last only with --all).
